{"changes":["cmd/telemetry.go (new): `eka telemetry emit --kind \u003ckind\u003e [--session \u003cid\u003e] [--subject] [--constraint] [--gate] [--reason]` appends exactly one record to docs/telemetry/\u003csessionId\u003e.jsonl. seq = last.seq+1 (0 for a new file) is the only ordering key; prevHash = hex SHA-256 of the previous record's raw bytes (\"\" first), so the chain is tamper-evident with no server state. A trailing CRLF is trimmed before hashing so the chain is stable across LF/CRLF checkouts. `telemetryAutoEmit` instruments the write/gate paths opt-in on a session id: publish success -\u003e first-write/write; conformance block, transition refusal, verify fail -\u003e gate-refusal; verify pass -\u003e gate-pass. Best-effort: it never changes a host command's exit code or output.","Session id is client-supplied (--session, else EKA_SESSION); EKA never mints-and-stores an id and never infers a session from timestamps. With neither, the record carries sessionId \"\" and sessionSource \"unattributed\".","docs/telemetry/*.jsonl is lifted as a source-only RSF attachment (ADR-027): .jsonl is neither .md nor .json, so the existing builder collects it verbatim into the snapshot; no builder change.","cmd/capture.go: `telemetry` added to captureTransportDirs so a telemetry file name never drives `eka capture` classification.","cmd/root.go, cmd/help_groups.go, cmd/help_groups_test.go: `eka telemetry` registered in the Runtime \u0026 Workspace group.","Single-writer per session file is documented (no platform locking): the session id is client-owned, so the client serialises; two concurrent emits to one session could duplicate seq."],"role":"implementation","summary":"Implemented the `eka telemetry` emit side (WI-A): an append-only per-session JSONL log with a prevHash chain, client-supplied sessionId semantics, opt-in auto-emit on the write and gate paths, a read-only read path, and source-only attachment transport — no store-schema, corpus, envelope or standard change.","tests":["go test ./cmd/ -run Telemetry -count=1 -\u003e ok (18 tests); gofmt -l cmd/ empty; go vet ./... and go build ./... clean; go test -timeout 1200s ./cmd/... ok.","Chain: TestTelemetryEmitAppendsAndChains asserts fixed field order, monotonic seq and prevHash=sha256(previous raw line). Non-vacuous: TestTelemetryEmitChainTamperFails flips to exit 1 ('chain broken', path:2) when a line is tampered.","CRLF: TestTelemetryCRLFChain emits over a CRLF-converted file (exit 0) and lists it; non-vacuous — removing the trim makes it exit 1 ('chain broken').","Read path: TestTelemetryReadsNeverWrite armed with EKA_SESSION=sess-read proves get/context create no docs/telemetry; non-vacuous when an emit is injected into the read path.","No-fabrication: TestTelemetryEmitUnattributed — two runs without a session id produce two records with sessionId \"\" (one file), no synthesized id.","Gate/kind: TestTelemetryEmitGateKind — gate-* requires --gate and non-gate kinds forbid it (exit 2); non-vacuous with the rule off.","Transport: TestTelemetryAttachmentRoundTrip (repo-relative id docs/telemetry/s1.jsonl, digest matches); TestTelemetryCaptureSkipList (non-vacuous without the skip-list).","Auto-emit: TestTelemetryAutoEmitTransitionRefusal / Verify / Publish PASS; without a session id nothing is written."]}